## 4. Two Competing Positions
- **Position A — Curated Plan-First Flow:** Users select a box size (5 or 10 meals) and a single dietary lane (e.g., High-Protein) first, and the menu narrows automatically. *Pro:* Fast checkout and predictable kitchen prep. *Con:* Restrictive for mixed dietary needs or ingredient-conscious buyers.
- **Position B — Filter-First A-La-Carte Builder:** Users land directly on the open weekly menu, apply multi-select allergen/macro filters, and fill a live box counter freely. *Pro:* High transparency and user control. *Con:* Higher risk of choice overload without clear grouping.

